        <div class="bf-vs-card"><h3>Bodyfriend vs. Ogawa</h3><p>Ogawa brings a refined Japanese-influence aesthetic and dual-engine design with the Master Drive Duo. Bodyfriend leans more futuristic Korean technology. Both are premium design brands — the difference is aesthetic direction and mechanism philosophy.</p></div>
        <div class="bf-vs-card"><h3>Bodyfriend vs. Fujiiryoki</h3><p>Fujiiryoki delivers authentic Japanese shiatsu heritage with a conservative, furniture-grade form factor. Bodyfriend is the futuristic opposite: Korean, tech-dominant, robotics-driven. Two very different philosophies, both executed at high quality.</p></div>
        <div class="bf-vs-card"><h3>Bodyfriend vs. Kyota</h3><p>Kyota focuses on wellness and a calmer, meditative massage therapeutic approach. Bodyfriend is technology-dominant with precision robotics. Kyota for therapeutic calm; Bodyfriend for precision technology and design.</p></div>
        <div class="bf-vs-card"><h3>Bodyfriend vs. Cozzia</h3><p>Cozzia offers a more accessible entry into premium massage with zero-gravity focus. Bodyfriend is distinctly premium-first, with a higher price floor and more advanced technology throughout the entire lineup.</p></div>
